WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:06.756
♪♪♪
- Oh, what's up, everybody? Peace. My name is Bobbito
García, aka

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:09.634
Kool. Bob. Love.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.596
Let's talk about what a point guard is.
♪♪♪

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.934
Excellence.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.395
The leader on the floor.

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:25.650
The coach for the coach.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:27.819
Let's elevate the title

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:31.865
to "point gods." The title that very few
have ever attained.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.744
I'm talkin' about Dwayne "Pearl" Washington,
aka Pac-Man. And I'm talking about

00:00:37.078 --> 00:00:39.289
[excitable screech] Shammgod.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:42.333
[Excitable screech] Kenny Anderson.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:46.546
[Excitable screech]
Future.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:50.091
Speedy. Bone. Professor. Come on now.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:54.679
All the point gods I just mentioned were
birthed here on the hallowed

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:56.806
asphalt of New York City.
[Car horns honking]

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.438
But let's go beyond

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:07.650
a Puerto Rico, the island of enchantment,
and recognize the point gods

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.152
de alla.
♪♪♪

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:13.740
There's

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.285
three players
who are kinda like los tres reyes.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:20.371
It's a holiday in Puerto Rico.
You understand?

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.291
They already legendary on the island.

00:01:23.708 --> 00:01:27.504
One had his number retired
on the national team.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:30.465
He goes by the name of Carlito Arroyo.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:34.928
Another recently retired as an NBA
champion.

00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:37.764
His name? J.J. Barea.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:39.933
And the

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:43.144
last but not least: The young one in the mix

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:46.397
who's about to create waves

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:49.609
and havoc in the NBA this upcoming season.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:53.404
He goes by the name of Jose Alvarado.

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:57.283
And this is "The Point Gods

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:02.205
de Puerto Ricooo!" Point Gods. PR.

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:04.958
Let's talk.

00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:10.922
- The end result,

00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:14.217
I think nobody believed, you know,
the way it went down.

00:02:14.425 --> 00:02:18.972
We scrimmaged USA at that summer before
the Olympics about three to four times.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:22.725
And the one thing that Larry Brown that
was the coach for that team.

00:02:22.725 --> 00:02:25.145
So they ask us to play,
you know, man-to-man

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:27.605
throughout the whole scrimmages
that we had.

00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:30.441
So our coaching staff was like,
"We're going to play zone the whole game."

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.945
You know? So we had an advantage

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:36.781
as far as preparation
when it came down to playing USA.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.993
But it was an amazing moment
for Puerto Rico basketball,

00:02:40.118 --> 00:02:42.495
for the history of basketball
in our island.

00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:45.123
To this day, they celebrate that day
like it's a birthday.

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:47.375
It was a team effort.

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:50.086
Everybody obviously did their part
for us to be able

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:53.047
to accomplish what we did
and we in the history books,

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:55.884
man. I'm truly honored
and blessed to be a part of that moment.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.553
We played with a lot of respect,
a lot of dignity because,

00:02:59.053 --> 00:02:59.971
you know, the fanbase

00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:02.974
that we have in Puerto Rico is not only in
the island—it's all around the world.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.268
Puerto Ricans,
they come out of everywhere, you know?

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:10.106
- Yeah.
- We got cousins and grandparents
and, you know, brothers everywhere.

00:03:10.106 --> 00:03:14.110
So it's truly an honor to just
represent the island the way we did.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:15.361
- So, J.J.,

00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:19.199
this is one of my favorite moments
in NBA history.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:23.870
I'm going to keep it 100 with you.
Because, and it's also historic,

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:27.957
not just for the league
but also for the franchise

00:03:27.957 --> 00:03:30.001
that you represented for so many years,

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:34.672
the Dallas Mavericks. In 2011,
during the Finals and Game 4,

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:38.009
the coaching staff decides to change

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:40.845
the starting lineup and insert you.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.764
That's crazy.

00:03:42.764 --> 00:03:45.850
I mean, that might happen
in the middle of a season, rare

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.437
for the playoffs,
but unheard of for the Finals.

00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:53.524
And the crazy thing is, after you started,
the Mavs didn't lose again.

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:55.860
Y'all won three in a row
and took the chip.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:01.115
Where were you when the coach shared
with you that you're starting?

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:04.827
- Yeah, I was driving home from practice
the day before

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:09.249
the game. And Coach calls me and says,
"Hey, we're gonna start you tomorrow.

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:12.001
We're gonna change things up.
And all we want you to do is

00:04:12.335 --> 00:04:15.129
grab the ball and attack the paint.
Try to find Dirk early."

00:04:15.171 --> 00:04:19.425
Like, I go home and I told my parents, "Yo,
I'm starting tomorrow in the NBA Finals."

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.639
So I had to find a way to stay as relaxed
as possible, but it worked out.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.392
So it was a great move by Coach.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:31.312
It was not easy to make that move.
But he made it, and it worked out for us.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:32.897
- So Jose, like,

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.151
you do something that's a little cuckoo.

00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:41.864
You know, like, if I was a coach,
you would be driving me crazy.

00:04:42.323 --> 00:04:46.536
Most people try to steal from behind in
the frontcourt on a fast break.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:51.666
You do it in the backcourt on the inbound

00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:55.586
or off of a change of possession.
- [Announcer:] Oh, from behind! Alvarado stole it.

00:04:58.548 --> 00:04:59.841
- What were the sidelines,

00:04:59.841 --> 00:05:00.883
what were your teammates, what were

00:05:00.883 --> 00:05:03.511
your coaches telling you? Like,
I'm sure they didn't approve.

00:05:05.263 --> 00:05:07.890
- I mean, it just happened naturally
when I was around, like, seventh

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.686
grade, eighth grade.
But I got in trouble for it for a while.

00:05:11.686 --> 00:05:15.481
You know, they were telling me
you would not make any team doing that.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.443
My college coach was like,
"If you do that, I'm subbing you out."
[Laughing]

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:23.573
- So I'm like. And in the NBA, coach
Willie Green really never said nothing to me.

00:05:23.573 --> 00:05:25.742
I think he didn't know
I was doing it at first.

00:05:25.742 --> 00:05:27.535
I think he was lost too.
I think he was just looking at up the floor,

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:29.620
so he couldn't really say

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.705
nothing at the time.

00:05:30.705 --> 00:05:32.874
But when I did do it, I was already,
the ball was stolen.

00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:34.292
So, he liked it.

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:35.376
He never told me nothing.

00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:37.795
Never told me nothing about it.
- [Announcer:] And this is what Alvarado does.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:39.922
- All right,

00:05:39.922 --> 00:05:40.965
well, the whole world knows.

00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:42.884
So it's something I'm gonna try to do
for the rest of my career.

00:05:42.884 --> 00:05:45.303
- He did it in Puerto Rico
and cost us a three.
- No, no, no, no, no.

00:05:45.762 --> 00:05:46.721
- Yup. Yes, you did.

00:05:46.721 --> 00:05:48.181
Yes, you did.
- No.

00:05:48.222 --> 00:05:48.806
- Yes, you did.

00:05:48.806 --> 00:05:50.433
I'm gonna send you the clip.

00:05:50.433 --> 00:05:52.060
- My thing right here,

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.021
I think I would have got Carlos and J.J.
with it. Carlos would've thought he was cool.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:58.232
You know, he wanna do all
these fancy things.

00:05:58.232 --> 00:06:01.778
- He'd be skippin' on the way down.
He'd be skippin' on the way down.

00:06:01.986 --> 00:06:04.447
- He would've never got me.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.116
He would've never got me.
- With his and-1s.
[Laughing]
- With my and-1s.

